  "content": [
    {
      "text": "Son of Jesus (also called Elymas), a Jew who had obtained an influence over Sergius Paulus, the Roman proconsul in Cyprus (Acts 13:6–12). He is called a sorcerer or magician and a false prophet. Paul destroyed his influence by calling down upon him a proof of the divine anger (Acts 13:11).",
